  "s18_conclusion": {
    "choice": "H1_FIRST_SELECTIVE_ACCEPTANCE",
    "why_minimum_justified_change": "H1 is the only axis that is simultaneously (a) directly implicated by the evidence, (b) achievable with ZERO training, ZERO checkpoint change, ZERO geometry change and ZERO fusion change, and (c) reversible. The frozen evidence shows the failure is an intervention-precision failure, not a representation failure: 122 GT-hit proposals already exist and 27 components are recovered with 0 losses, so the localizer does produce usable targets. What is missing is a mechanism to decline the 372 off-target proposals, and the off-target support fraction is the strongest descriptor of the FP burden (rho 0.5918-0.6372, consistent across all four architectures). The score, although saturated, retains moderate discriminative information (ROC-AUC 0.670611), and every label-blind marginal floor removes strictly more off-target than GT-hit proposals (q10 removes 50 off-target and 0 hits). H2 would change the model weights before establishing whether the existing weights are the limiting factor, and H3 would confound the analysis by changing the fusion rule while the accept/reject policy is still untested. H1 is therefore the lowest-complexity intervention capable of testing a credible explanation of the Phase-13 failure.",
